    "summary": "Genestealer Cults errata replacing Cult Ambush in full. For a GENESTEALER CULTS Army Faction, the battle begins with Resurgence points set by battle size: 6 at Incursion, 10 at Strike Force, 14 at Onslaught. When one of your units is destroyed and all of its non-CHARACTER models have this ability, you may pay Resurgence points set by its Starting Strength, ignoring attached CHARACTER models: Aberrants cost 4 at 5 models or 8 at 10; Hybrid Metamorphs, and Acolyte Hybrids units armed with autopistols or hand flamers, cost 2 at 5 or 4 at 10; Atalan Jackals cost 2 at 5 or 6 at 10; Neophyte Hybrids cost 3 at 10 or 6 at 20; Purestrain Genestealers cost 2 at 5 or 6 at 10. Paying adds a full-strength copy of that unit, without its CHARACTER models, to your army, held in Cult Ambush with every wound intact and [ONE SHOT] weapons treated as unfired, and you set down one Cult Ambush marker at a spot where every enemy unit is over 8\" away horizontally, or skip the marker when no such spot exists. Cult Ambush counts as Strategic Reserves: those units cannot be picked for the Rapid Ingress Stratagem, may arrive through a marker or by the usual Strategic Reserves rules on a later turn, and are not destroyed automatically after battle round three. Markers are 32mm circles, and a marker is removed once an enemy model other than AIRCRAFT finishes moving, by any means, within 8\" of that marker. When your opponent's following Movement phase ends, each remaining marker lets one of your units in Cult Ambush make an ingress move, set up with a model touching that marker and every other model wholly within 3\" of it; the marker is then removed. These ingress moves are allowed in battle round one.",
